    "story": {
      "type": "creator-story",
      "settings": {
        "color_scheme": "default",
        "panel_color": "#f4f1ec",
        "heading_plain": "Why I",
        "heading_serif": "teach drawing",
        "underline_color": "#5ec3ea",
        "text": "<p>I stopped drawing at eleven, when a teacher held my picture up as the one not to copy. I started again at twenty nine, on a train, in the back of a work notebook.</p><p>Since then I have filled a shelf of sketchbooks, taught workshops in libraries and cafés, and written a book about the ten minutes before breakfast that changed how I see.</p><p>Everything I have learned is on this site. Most of it is free, and it will stay that way.</p>",
        "link_label": "Read the full story",
        "link": "/pages/about",
        "image_1": "shopify://shop_images/creator-desk-sketches.webp",
        "image_1_alt": "Small ink sketches filling a page beside a keyboard",
        "image_2": "shopify://shop_images/creator-pillow-sketches.webp",
        "image_2_alt": "Pencil studies of cushions in a spiral sketchbook",
        "image_3": "shopify://shop_images/creator-morning-desk.webp",
        "image_3_alt": "A small drawing on a wooden desk with pens and a bowl of oranges",
        "thread_color": "#f6a27c",
        "button_color": "#5ec3ea",
        "button_text_color": "#1c1b2b"
      },
